# s17_if_region.tkr — §17 conditional-compilation region prune. A single #if/#elseif/#else/#endif
# region defines `pick` four times; the build-time prune keeps exactly the arm the target satisfies
# (first-true-wins), so the build has no duplicate definition. The leading #if(os == "windows") arm
# calls a NONEXISTENT symbol and, on the linux host, is pruned before type-check without error —
# proving the prune precedes the checker. On linux the #elseif(os == "linux") arm survives, so `pick`
# returns 42.

Feature: §17 #if region prune — exactly the target's arm survives, pruned arms never reach the checker

  Scenario: linux_arm_survives — on linux the #elseif(os == "linux") arm returns 42, other arms pruned
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 42
